Dependencies make names visible. A source dependency path resolves from the binding file's owning module root, not its directory.

- `@card render_card` at the start of a statement is a dependency clause. It binds `render_card`.
- `@settings site_name` inside an expression reads one value without binding it.
- `@docs/intro.mtf` is a file value that produces a `String`.

### Module-root-relative paths

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    @card render_card
    @markdown render

    title = @settings site_name
    intro = @docs/intro.mtf
]

`@card` resolves under the owning module root. `@markdown` can name an accessible scoped support package. A `.moth` file has no file value.

Root filenames such as `@mod.moth` and `@entry.moth` cannot be dependency targets. Cross-module imports see only names marked by `$export` in the applicable facade.

See @#dependency-paths (Dependency paths).
